<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2681" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">annŏtātĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adn-</span></b> ),
			ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				noting down in writing</i>, <i>a remark</i>, <i>annotation</i> (post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">a te librum meum cum adnotationibus tuis
					exspecto,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 7, 20</span></i>
			; Gell. praef.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Esp. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> In the
			jurists, <i>the registering of a person among the
				accused</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 48, 17,
			4</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A rescript of the emperor</i>, <i>signed with his own hand</i>, Cod. Th. Fragm. 1, 2, 1.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
